{"id": "EUVD-2026-41495", "enisaUuid": "53ffc11a-0ae7-37ce-9568-35693a806b1d", "description": "When a libcurl-based application performs transfers via `SCP://` or `SFTP://`\nand utilizes the `CURLOPT_SSH_KEYFUNCTION` callback, it may silently accept an\nuntrusted server. This vulnerability occurs when a server presents a host key\ntype that does not match the specific key type already recorded for that host\nin the `known_hosts` file. Instead of rejecting the mismatch, the callback\nmechanism fails to properly enforce the restriction, allowing the connection\nto succeed without warning and risking a potential man-in-the-middle attack.", "datePublished": "2026-07-03T06:18:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-15T06:03:34", "baseScore": 7.4, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N", "references": ["https://curl.se/docs/CVE-2026-9547.json", "https://curl.se/docs/CVE-2026-9547.html", "https://hackerone.com/reports/3751712"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-9547", "GHSA-xq9p-gxg6-f7q6"], "assigner": "curl", "epss": 0.33, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0186aa65-02f6-3e1d-a344-6dc06f3944c4", "product": {"name": "curl", "vendor": {"name": "curl"}}, "product_version": "8.9.0"}, {"id": "07f1101b-6669-3d53-8f8a-b90e5147f382", "product": {"name": "curl", "vendor": {"name": "curl"}}, "product_version": "8.1.1"}, {"id": "08be1122-4aa2-3904-94df-17776e8d7beb", "product": {"name": "curl", "vendor": {"name": "curl"}}, "product_version": "8.14.1"}, {"id": "1119b99c-9135-33b7-b77c-decc2c112fc3", "product": {"name": "curl", "vendor": {"name": "curl"}}, "product_version": "7.71.1"}, {"id": "149792ba-564b-3ea2-93cc-1a71d71d4df0", "product": {"name": "curl", "vendor": {"name": "curl"}}, "product_version": "7.78.0"}, {"id": "1d456c04-0184-3494-b6a8-9b7b524bcb0e", "product": {"name": "curl", "vendor": {"name": "curl"}}, "product_version": "8.15.0 <8.16.1"}, {"id": "1ffc8bfa-f8c3-3fb7-af55-22cf47ccf294", "product": {"name": "curl", "vendor": {"name": "curl"}}, "p